---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const description =
  'The mybankjobs privacy policy, for the website and the iOS app: no accounts, no tracking, and everything you type stays on your device.';
---

<Base title="Privacy — mybankjobs" description={description} narrow>
  <a class="backlink" href="/">← All vacancies</a>
  <div class="prose">
  <h1>Privacy</h1>

  <p class="lede">
    mybankjobs has no accounts, asks for no personal details, and has nothing to log you into. This
    page covers both the website and the mybankjobs iOS app.
  </p>

  <h2>The iOS app</h2>
  <p>
    The app collects nothing. Your saved jobs, your “find your fit” answers, and your visit history
    live only on your device, and deleting the app deletes them. The app talks to our servers for
    exactly one reason: to download the public vacancy listings — the same anonymous requests your
    browser makes when it opens this website. No identifier, account, or analytics event travels
    with them.
  </p>
  <p>
    Applying always happens on the bank's own official website, which has its own privacy policy —
    nothing you enter there passes through us.
  </p>

  <h2>The website</h2>
  <p>
    No accounts, no cookies, no tracking. At most we use privacy-friendly, cookieless analytics to
    count page views in aggregate — never anything that identifies you. What you type into search or
    “find your fit” stays in your browser.
  </p>
  <p>
    Browser notifications are the one exception, and only if you switch them on. When you do, your
    browser hands us an anonymous delivery address — a push endpoint plus two encryption keys — and
    that is all we store. It doesn't tell us who you are, and nothing is attached to it: no email,
    no name, no history of what you looked at. Turn notifications off and we delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>
    Anything unclear, or want something checked or removed? Email
    <a href="mailto:tebellonamo@gmail.com">tebellonamo@gmail.com</a> — requests are honoured promptly.
  </p>
  </div>
</Base>
